.TH "listNodes" "1" "" "SequoiaDB User Manuals" ""
.hy
.PP
#NAME#
.PP
listNodes - list node information
.PP
#SYNOPSIS#
.PP
\f[B]oma.listNodes([options], [filter])\f[R]
.PP
#CATEGORY#
.PP
Oma
.PP
#DESCRIPTION#
.PP
This function is used to list the eligible node information of the current sdbcm
machine.
It displays the information of data node, coord node and catalog node by
default.
.PP
#PARAMETERS#
.IP \[bu] 2
options ( \f[I]object, optional\f[R] )
.RS 2
.PP
Specify the node type, mode and other parameters through the parameter
\[lq]options\[rq]:
.IP \[bu] 2
type ( \f[I]string\f[R] ): Node type, and the default is \[lq]db\[rq]
.RS 2
.PP
The values are as follows:
.IP \[bu] 2
\[lq]all\[rq]: All nodes
.IP \[bu] 2
\[lq]db\[rq]: data node, coord node and catalog node
.IP \[bu] 2
\[lq]om\[rq]: sdbom node
.IP \[bu] 2
\[lq]cm\[rq]: sdbcm node
.PP
Format: \f[C]type: \[dq]all\[dq]\f[R]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
mode ( \f[I]string\f[R] ): Node mode, and the default is \[lq]run\[rq]
.RS 2
.PP
The values are as follows:
.IP \[bu] 2
\[lq]run\[rq]: Running node
.IP \[bu] 2
\[lq]local\[rq]: Local node, whether it is running or not
.PP
Format: \f[C]mode: \[dq]local\[dq]\f[R]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
role ( \f[I]string\f[R] ): Node role
.RS 2
.PP
The values are as follows:
.IP \[bu] 2
\[lq]data\[rq]: data node
.IP \[bu] 2
\[lq]coord\[rq]: coord node
.IP \[bu] 2
\[lq]catalog\[rq]: catalog node
.IP \[bu] 2
\[lq]standalone\[rq]: standalone node
.IP \[bu] 2
\[lq]om\[rq]: sdbom node
.IP \[bu] 2
\[lq]cm\[rq]: sdbcm node
.PP
Format: \f[C]role: \[dq]data\[dq]\f[R]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
svcname ( \f[I]string\f[R] ): Node port number
.RS 2
.PP
When specifying multiple svcnames, separate them with a comma (,).
.PP
Format: \f[C]svcname: \[dq]11820, 11830\[dq]\f[R]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
showalone ( \f[I]boolean\f[R] )\[uFF1A]Whether to display the sdbcm node
information started in standalone mode, and the default is false.
.RS 2
.PP
Format: \f[C]standalone: true\f[R]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
expand ( \f[I]boolean\f[R] ): Whether to display the extended information of the
node, and the default is false.
.RS 2
.PP
Format: \f[C]expand: true\f[R]
.RE
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
filter ( \f[I]object, optional\f[R] )
.RS 2
.PP
Specify the conditions for filtering node information.
It supports to retrieve the node information through matching symbol $and, $or,
$not or exact match.
.RE
.PP
#RETURN VALUE#
.PP
When the function executes successfully, it will return an object of type
BSONArray.
Users can get a list of node details through this object.
