.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
.PP
#ERRORS#
.PP
When the exception happens, use getLastErrMsg() to get the error message or use
getLastError() to get the error code.
For more details, refer to Troubleshooting.
.PP
#VERSION#
.PP
v2.0 and above
.PP
#EXAMPLES#
.PP
Connect to the local cluster management service process sdbcm to obtain
information of the node 11830.
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
> var oma = new Oma(\[dq]localhost\[dq], 11790)
> oma.listNodes({svcname: \[dq]11830\[dq]})
{
  \[dq]svcname\[dq]: \[dq]11830\[dq],
  \[dq]type\[dq]: \[dq]sequoiadb\[dq],
  \[dq]role\[dq]: \[dq]data\[dq],
  \[dq]pid\[dq]: 17984,
  \[dq]groupid\[dq]: 1001,
  \[dq]nodeid\[dq]: 1001,
  \[dq]primary\[dq]: 1,
  \[dq]isalone\[dq]: 0,
  \[dq]groupname\[dq]: \[dq]group2\[dq],
  \[dq]starttime\[dq]: \[dq]2021-07-15-16.27.47\[dq],
  \[dq]dbpath\[dq]: \[dq]/opt/sequoiadb/database/data/11830/\[dq]
}
\f[R]
.fi
